  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The heading printed over a reading from a book named by its title. LÉCTIO is the nominative of a heading: no verb is expressed or understood. LIBRI is the genitive of liber (book), and the second genitive is the title of the book. APOCALÝPSIS is the title of the book; BEÁTI agrees with IOÁNNIS, which depends on it, with APÓSTOLI in apposition.",
    "source": {
      "method": "The Latin follows the Benziger Brothers 1962 editio iuxta typicam, which prints this heading over the Epistle on printed p. 726 (IA leaf n807 / PDF p. 808) and over the 4 further readings named in the witness header; it is compared with the heading line of the pinned Divinum Officium file that the reading's own digital witness binds. Source review remains pending.",
